    "narrative": "For September 13th, our lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (78.67) and **James Wood** (74.47), who stand as our premier plays due to their elite combination of speed-based upside and favorable matchups. **Corbin Carroll** capitalizes on Cal Quantrill\u2019s notoriously slow delivery, providing the highest projected steal efficiency of the day, while **James Wood** benefits from an elite 0.415 xwOBA and an aggressive lead-off spot against a porous matchup. We are also high on **Mickey Moniak** (74.24), who is seeing a massive 14% boost from a favorable platoon advantage, and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.57), whose strong 17% SP skill adjustment against Bubba Chandler cements him as an essential start. **Josh Naylor** (71.58) rounds out our top tier, as the 10% park factor adjustment significantly elevates his floor despite the lefty-on-lefty encounter.\n\nThe tightest decision on the bench involved **Brice Turang**, whose 51.74 score made him the primary candidate for a utility spot. While **Brice Turang** holds high intrinsic value due to his stolen base profile, the optimizer favored **Austin Riley** (58.62) and **Zach McKinstry** (50.35) due to superior raw volume and park-adjusted base projections against their respective opponents. **Jose Caballero** (46.25) remained on the bench due to a poor lineup projection (#9) and a significant 13% penalty against the platoon, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** (42.18) was excluded entirely due to the double-whammy of a tough SP matchup and a negative platoon split.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, as nearly every slot relies on assumed lineup positioning. While **Gabriel Moreno** (63.24) and **Isaac Paredes** (59.17) carry high upside, they are contingent on maintaining their projected spots in the order; any move down the lineup will erode their current efficiency scores. Investors should keep a close watch on weather reports, as the aggregate base projections for **Cole Young** (58.88) and **Max Muncy** (55.56) are sensitive to stadium-specific volatility. With **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** also waiting in the wings, we have the flexibility to pivot if any of our starters are scratched prior to first pitch.",
